WEBVTT

00:00:05.450 --> 00:00:10.000
<v Priya Raman>Morning, everyone. Can you hear me? Teams has picked the wrong microphone again.</v>

00:00:11.580 --> 00:00:20.329
<v Fiona Doyle>Yeah, you're coming through. I was just looking at the weather for the weekend. Had plans for a walk, but apparently we're getting properly soaked.</v>

00:00:21.030 --> 00:00:28.030
<v Tomasz Nowak>We got that this morning. Traffic on the ring road was barely moving. Twenty minutes looking at the same van.</v>

00:00:28.769 --> 00:00:31.219
<v Sarah Okafor>Lovely. A scenic tour, without the scenery.</v>

00:00:32.829 --> 00:00:41.579
<v Tomasz Nowak>And now the heating in the portakabin is roasting me. Not asking anyone to fix it, before that becomes a job. Just having a moan.</v>

00:00:42.149 --> 00:00:44.950
<v Olumide Adeyemi>That's your temperature compensation. Cold outside, tropical inside.</v>

00:00:46.259 --> 00:00:52.909
<v Priya Raman>Right, Tuesday, sixth of October. Let's get through the actual list before we lose everyone to the portakabin sauna.</v>

00:00:55.229 --> 00:01:01.530
<v Priya Raman>First, I finished the repair on the trucks last night. That's done, not something we're carrying into today.</v>

00:01:03.310 --> 00:01:08.909
<v Fiona Doyle>And I already swapped the filter on the 11kV board yesterday. That one's finished as well.</v>

00:01:09.620 --> 00:01:14.519
<v Sarah Okafor>Good. Those were still showing in the chat history, so worth saying they're closed.</v>

00:01:16.109 --> 00:01:21.709
<v Tomasz Nowak>Same for mine: finished the repair on the line 1 mould temp last night. All done.</v>

00:01:22.620 --> 00:01:25.769
<v Priya Raman>Cheers. Three completed bits, then, no repeat jobs there.</v>

00:01:27.840 --> 00:01:34.840
<v Marcus Hale>Just an observation from me. Heard a slight rattle from the Line 3 Screw and Barrel, nothing to action yet.</v>

00:01:35.989 --> 00:01:44.040
<v Aisha Begum>Yeah, and I heard a slight rattle from the line 1 hydraulics. Same thing, nothing to action yet. Just mentioning what I heard.</v>

00:01:44.980 --> 00:01:49.530
<v Priya Raman>Understood. Observations only, neither of those is becoming a new job this morning.</v>

00:01:50.920 --> 00:01:57.219
<v Tomasz Nowak>The other thing, the supplier still hasn't confirmed the delivery for the main water valve. That's still blocked.</v>

00:01:57.739 --> 00:02:02.989
<v Fiona Doyle>Yeah, there's no confirmed delivery against it. Still a blocker, not fresh work for today.</v>

00:02:05.439 --> 00:02:13.840
<v Aisha Begum>And we were going to replace the belt on the PRV on the boiler, but that's been pushed to next month, so ignore it.</v>

00:02:14.159 --> 00:02:18.710
<v Priya Raman>Fine, that replacement is off this round. Right, onto what we are agreeing.</v>

00:02:20.129 --> 00:02:24.330
<v Priya Raman>I'll inspect the MV01 for leaks today. I'll take that one myself.</v>

00:02:25.590 --> 00:02:31.189
<v Sarah Okafor>Just the leak inspection, yeah? Not agreeing a replacement off the back of the old note?</v>

00:02:32.110 --> 00:02:36.659
<v Priya Raman>Exactly. Inspect the MV01 for leaks today, nothing beyond that being agreed here.</v>

00:02:37.039 --> 00:02:39.840
<v Fiona Doyle>Got it, Priya Raman against that inspection today.</v>

00:02:42.240 --> 00:02:47.840
<v Priya Raman>Aisha, can you take vibration readings on the feedwater pump tomorrow at 9:30? Top priority please.</v>

00:02:49.870 --> 00:02:53.370
<v Aisha Begum>Sorry, you clipped slightly. Tomorrow at 9:30, not this morning?</v>

00:02:55.639 --> 00:02:59.139
<v Priya Raman>Tomorrow at 9:30, yes. And that is top priority please.</v>

00:03:01.050 --> 00:03:07.000
<v Aisha Begum>Yep, accepted. I'll take vibration readings on the feedwater pump tomorrow at 9:30. Top of my list.</v>

00:03:07.680 --> 00:03:12.580
<v Marcus Hale>I heard this morning as well, to be fair. The audio went all underwater.</v>

00:03:13.990 --> 00:03:16.789
<v Aisha Begum>Good, not just me needing another coffee, then.</v>

00:03:18.430 --> 00:03:25.080
<v Priya Raman>Tom, can you update the risk assessment for work on the waste heat boiler by Thursday? Top priority please.</v>

00:03:26.879 --> 00:03:32.129
<v Tomasz Nowak>Yeah. We're talking the risk assessment for the work, not rewriting the whole operating document?</v>

00:03:33.520 --> 00:03:39.120
<v Priya Raman>That's right, the risk assessment for work on the waste heat boiler. Keeping it to that.</v>

00:03:39.969 --> 00:03:44.169
<v Tomasz Nowak>Okay, I'll update that risk assessment by Thursday. Understood on top priority.</v>

00:03:44.919 --> 00:03:51.219
<v Fiona Doyle>Thursday for that, and tomorrow at 9:30 for the readings. Two separate dates; I've got them straight now.</v>

00:03:51.789 --> 00:03:54.939
<v Priya Raman>Yes, exactly. Both with the priority we've just said.</v>

00:03:55.639 --> 00:04:01.939
<v Priya Raman>Sarah Okafor, can you write up the near miss at the line two for Monday? It's fairly important.</v>

00:04:03.740 --> 00:04:11.439
<v Sarah Okafor>I can't take that on, sorry. I haven't got the capacity to give the write-up proper attention. Better to say no now.</v>

00:04:11.969 --> 00:04:20.019
<v Priya Raman>Okay. Marcus, can I hand that to you instead? Write up the near miss at the line two for Monday. Still fairly important.</v>

00:04:21.490 --> 00:04:27.439
<v Marcus Hale>Yeah, I'll take it instead. I'll write up the near miss at the line two for Monday.</v>

00:04:28.250 --> 00:04:33.850
<v Sarah Okafor>Thanks. Sorry to bounce it, but I don't want my name against something I can't do.</v>

00:04:34.930 --> 00:04:41.230
<v Marcus Hale>No, fair enough. I've already got my notes from it, so I'm not starting with a blank page.</v>

00:04:42.029 --> 00:04:45.529
<v Priya Raman>Thanks, Marcus. That's yours, then, for Monday, and fairly important.</v>

00:04:47.970 --> 00:04:54.620
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Um, on Northfield, I'll do a site visit at Northfield with the contractor on Friday. Low priority, that one.</v>

00:04:55.170 --> 00:04:59.370
<v Fiona Doyle>Friday, with the contractor. And low priority, rather than being pulled forward?</v>

00:05:00.370 --> 00:05:06.319
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Exactly. I'll do the site visit at Northfield with the contractor on Friday. It stays low priority.</v>

00:05:07.949 --> 00:05:12.149
<v Priya Raman>Thanks, Olumide Adeyemi. Agreed as you've said it: on Friday, low priority.</v>

00:05:14.240 --> 00:05:18.089
<v Tomasz Nowak>Take the portakabin weather with you. You'll have sunshine all day.</v>

00:05:19.389 --> 00:05:22.889
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Think that's just the heater and a fluorescent tube, mate.</v>

00:05:24.600 --> 00:05:33.699
<v Aisha Begum>I'll organise the toolbox talk for the team this afternoon as well. That's in the 'if you've got a spare minute' category, not another top-priority one.</v>

00:05:34.970 --> 00:05:41.620
<v Priya Raman>Thanks, Aisha. Yes, if you've got a spare minute; we're not giving that the same urgency as the readings.</v>

00:05:43.490 --> 00:05:48.389
<v Aisha Begum>Yep. I'll organise it this afternoon on that basis. Just keeping the urgency clear.</v>

00:05:49.689 --> 00:05:53.889
<v Sarah Okafor>Fine by me. No need to turn everything into a red flag.</v>

00:05:54.829 --> 00:06:02.529
<v Priya Raman>There's also the pressure drop on the GT2 Inlet Water Injection Valve. That needs investigating, normal priority. Anyone able to take it?</v>

00:06:04.699 --> 00:06:09.250
<v Marcus Hale>I can't take that investigation as well, sorry. Don't put it against me.</v>

00:06:10.319 --> 00:06:16.620
<v Olumide Adeyemi>I can't commit to that one either. Don't want a vague 'I'll have a look' turning into ownership.</v>

00:06:18.449 --> 00:06:21.600
<v Tomasz Nowak>Same here, no capacity for that on top. Sorry.</v>

00:06:21.899 --> 00:06:29.600
<v Priya Raman>Right. Investigate the pressure drop on the GT2 Inlet Water Injection Valve stays unassigned, normal priority. No owner and no date agreed.</v>

00:06:32.050 --> 00:06:34.850
<v Fiona Doyle>Yes, unallocated. Not tucked under somebody else's name.</v>

00:06:36.279 --> 00:06:42.230
<v Priya Raman>Okay, that's the list. Anything we've just discussed that I've misunderstood? Not opening a second list, mind.</v>

00:06:43.360 --> 00:06:47.560
<v Sarah Okafor>No, all clear. And we nearly managed that without everyone talking over—</v>

00:06:48.160 --> 00:06:54.110
<v Fiona Doyle>—each other. Sorry! No, nothing from me. Back to deciding whether my weekend walk needs a canoe.</v>

00:06:56.170 --> 00:07:01.420
<v Tomasz Nowak>I'll be here slowly turning into a baked potato. Again, commentary, not a maintenance request.</v>

00:07:03.550 --> 00:07:07.750
<v Priya Raman>Very clearly recorded as a moan. Cheers, everyone, we'll leave it there.</v>

00:07:08.370 --> 00:07:09.569
<v Marcus Hale>Cheers. Bye.</v>
